fuse: a directory the guest made lists itself

After 0044 the last round trips of reading a tree the guest had just made
were its listings: fifteen thousand READDIRs over node_modules straight
after the install, on the M1.

A complete directory (0044) lists itself from the dcache. The listing is a
snapshot taken when the stream starts, at opendir or rewinddir, kept on the
open file and read with positions of its own. POSIX lets a stream reflect
the directory as it was then; what it must not do is mix those positions
with the server's, which a shared cache torn down mid-stream would. So this
stream reads nothing else, and a directory no longer complete is asked of
the server at its next rewind.

